From 853f7d0208813c446365255f50da719bc2c9e0ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelpro09_Dev <aloplop090708@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 14:59:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix low-res photo bug via raw YUV JPEG bypass

MiuiCamera depends on the proprietary vendor.xiaomi.hardware.campostproc
HIDL service (MiaInterface/MiCameraAlgo) to finish processing captures in
every mode except UltraHD/108MP. That service is genuinely absent on this
AOSP port (declared optional in the framework compat matrix, never
shipped for third-party use), so dispatchTask always fails and the app
is left with only the GPU preview-readback placeholder (~1.6MP) as the
final photo, with the processing state stuck forever.

This adds lunaris.camerafix.RawJpegFix, hooked into two points:
- id.h0$i.onImageAvailable (CAM_PostProcessor): the universal raw
  YUV_420_888 delivery point for all modes but UltraHD. Caches the raw
  Image and hands off to an async worker (debounced per capture burst).
- com.android.camera.Camera.Ke (onCreate): calls RawJpegFix.preload(),
  which warms up JIT/class-loading on a background thread well before
  any capture, so the real hook stays a near-free invoke-static call
  on this timing-sensitive callback.

The worker thread:
- Converts the YUV_420_888 buffer to NV21 by hand (plane-stride aware),
  fixing a U/V-swap present in this device's Qualcomm HAL output.
- Resolves the real capture rotation and lens facing by matching the
  image dimensions against every camera's
  CameraCharacteristics.SENSOR_INFO_ACTIVE_ARRAY_SIZE, then rotates the
  NV21 buffer in software (no EXIF is written by YuvImage, so the
  rotation must be applied to the pixel data itself).
- Encodes to JPEG and, for the front camera specifically, upscales 2x
  (the front OV16A1Q sensor is exposed by this HAL build only in its
  2x2-binned 2304x1728 mode; native stream configs never advertise the
  full 4608x3456/16MP readout).
- Publishes the result through MediaStore's own pending-file API
  (ContentResolver.openOutputStream + IS_PENDING=0), rather than
  guessing at the placeholder's filesystem path: the row inserted by
  ParallelProcessProvider stays in .pending-<ts>-<name> form until then,
  which is why naive path-based matching always missed it.
- Clears the stuck row from
  com.xiaomi.camera.parallelservice.provider.SpecialTypesProvider so
  Gallery's CheckPostProcessing stops reporting the photo as
  processing forever.
